# Saturn
#
# Present only to raise tides on Enceladus. Saturn's own tidal response does
# not matter here and is given a large Q so that it does essentially nothing.

sName         saturn       # Body's name
saModules     eqtide       # List of modules to apply to this body

# Physical Parameters (JPL planetary physical parameters)
dMass         5.6834e26    # Mass, in kg
dRadius       58232        # Equatorial radius, in km
dRadGyra      0.22         # Radius of gyration
dRotPeriod    0.4440       # Rotation period, in days (10.656 h)
dObliquity    26.73        # Obliquity

# EQTIDE Parameters
dTidalQ       1e5          # Tidal Q (Saturn's dissipation is not the subject here)
dK2           0.39         # Love number of degree 2
saTidePerts   enceladus    # Names of perturbing bodies
